  "help": "<section id=\"help\"><h2>Opening things on this drive</h2><div class=\"columns\"><div><h3>On a computer</h3><p>Guides and books are PDFs. They open in any web browser.</p>{{desktop}}</div><div><h3>On an Android phone or tablet</h3><p>PDFs open from the Files app.</p>{{android}}</div><div><h3>On an iPhone or iPad</h3><p>PDFs open in the Files app with no extra software.</p><p>Wikipedia and the other big archives need the free <strong>Kiwix</strong> app. Install it from the App Store while you have internet; an iPhone cannot install an app from a drive.</p></div></div><div class=\"notice static-only\"><strong>If tapping a link does nothing</strong><p>Some phone previews show this page but will not follow its links. Each item lists where it is on the drive. Close this preview, open the drive in your Files app, and follow those folders to the file.</p></div></section>",
  "help_readers": "<p>Wikipedia and the other big archives open with the free <strong>Kiwix</strong> app. It is on this drive:</p><ul>{{links}}</ul><p>In Kiwix, choose “Open file” and pick an archive from the drive’s <code>LIBRARY/ZIM</code> folder. If an archive is in several parts, keep the parts together and open the first.</p>",
  "help_no_readers": "<p>The big archives on this drive open with the free <strong>Kiwix</strong> app. It is not on this drive; install it while you have internet.</p>"
